From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chinmoy Dey <chinmoy@nexthop.ai>
Date: Fri, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Advertise canonical Chassis LeakDetectors collection

The rmc-events integration (patch 0005) serves the LeakDetector
collection at both the canonical Chassis-level URI
(/redfish/v1/Chassis/<id>/LeakDetectors, LeakDetection v1.2.0 /
Chassis v1.26.0+) and the deprecated nested URI under
ThermalSubsystem/LeakDetection, and links the deprecated tree from
ThermalSubsystem. The canonical collection, however, was not reachable
by navigation: the Chassis resource did not advertise it.

Add the standard navigation link, as upstream does for every other
child resource, so the canonical leak-detection tree is discoverable
like a normal Redfish resource. Chassis.LeakDetectors is a property
defined by the DMTF Chassis schema (since v1.26.0), which the pinned
bmcweb bundles.

 * chassis.hpp: advertise the canonical Chassis-level LeakDetectors
   collection (/redfish/v1/Chassis/<id>/LeakDetectors).

This patch only adds a link property to an existing handler; it adds
no new routes (those come from patch 0005).

Author: Chinmoy Dey <chinmoy@nexthop.ai>
---
 redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp b/redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp
index 00000001..00000002 100644
--- a/redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp
+++ b/redfish-core/lib/chassis.hpp
@@ -450,9 +450,14 @@
     asyncResp->res.jsonValue["Assembly"]["@odata.id"] =
         boost::urls::format("/redfish/v1/Chassis/{}/Assembly", chassisId);

     // SensorCollection
     asyncResp->res.jsonValue["Sensors"]["@odata.id"] =
         boost::urls::format("/redfish/v1/Chassis/{}/Sensors", chassisId);
+
+    // LeakDetectorCollection (canonical location, Chassis v1.26.0+)
+    asyncResp->res.jsonValue["LeakDetectors"]["@odata.id"] =
+        boost::urls::format("/redfish/v1/Chassis/{}/LeakDetectors", chassisId);
+
     asyncResp->res.jsonValue["Status"]["State"] = resource::State::Enabled;

     nlohmann::json::array_t computerSystems;
